{"id": "clm:9a16f50966d646b8b260ce371c58afad38c952c5906a55e187aef808f76878d9", "type": "statement", "text": "Increasing batch size may enable capture, but can delay the first response and increase unnecessary I/O when clients do not consume all results. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0fc3aac0fa1393a8e789f707c9d1fe9d122397f8bf193bf988e8da3ba4630d31"]}
{"id": "clm:d86182276f047f9d7868fec98641152b45a4b59f777bd489f437e974ae48bf4f", "type": "statement", "text": "Enable profiling through a custom cluster parameter group and separately enable the cluster's profiler log export; configuring only one side does not deliver logs. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pabis.eu/blog/2023-10-31-AWS-DocumentDB-Profiling.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e04aeb50daee6ea51233c42875691205bbf4a0161a79228ad1b6a13192147aa1"]}
{"id": "clm:9b4140928cf7ebbbf585d9792c9bee9d9fc2b1a8bae623356430af17e62e22a5", "type": "statement", "text": "AWS documents query-log coverage only when the entire result fits in one batch and remains under 16 MB. Increasing batch size can improve capture but delay the first response and waste I/O when results are discarded. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0fc3aac0fa1393a8e789f707c9d1fe9d122397f8bf193bf988e8da3ba4630d31"]}
{"id": "clm:0fff697c86d320fd04d1be75e366d5b5ce0b8e572f4e44d14ce7b2d5fc6d08c7", "type": "statement", "text": "Pabis demonstrates a low-traffic DocumentDB 4.0 test with a 50 ms threshold, sampling 1.0, and Terraform-enabled profiler exports. AWS recommends starting with a high threshold and lowering it gradually; it warns that 50 ms can cause performance issues for high-throughput applications, so the Pabis configuration should not be treated as a general default for those workloads. (low confidence) Sources: https://pabis.eu/blog/2023-10-31-AWS-DocumentDB-Profiling.html ; https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "source_url": "https://pabis.eu/blog/2023-10-31-AWS-DocumentDB-Profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION", "evidence_ids": [], "remediation": {"schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1", "record": "remediation.json", "requires_revalidation": true, "claim_text_sha256": "c0f93f7ea4b06a0c49f1dccc14911dfdca6a290f1ec0a77ad84f2f85899f0e3e"}, "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "origin_evidence_ids": ["ev:6d3157cee87994106d5f250175a33f0dfe1b6c87846896e41445fcbcf7cbe958", "ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:865276c223bac79bb52c32ba9f585994880d71287937f7fdf73ac5dd86dfa156", "type": "statement", "text": "Amazon DocumentDB's profiler captures slow database operations above a configured duration threshold and exports their execution details to CloudWatch Logs for investigation. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pabis.eu/blog/2023-10-31-AWS-DocumentDB-Profiling.html", "https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:d60cbeef26ddd2f84ac9880a810df66c4b2d404d040a66cea6c218430df810a3", "type": "statement", "text": "Plan summaries such as COLLSCAN help connect slow operations to missing indexes; in an AWS example, adding indexes replaced COLLSCANs with IXSCANs and cut query runtime. Sources: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/performance-slow-queries.md ; https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/profiling-slow-running-queries-in-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/performance-slow-queries.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/", "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/profiling-slow-running-queries-in-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION", "evidence_ids": [], "remediation": {"schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1", "record": "remediation.json", "requires_revalidation": true, "claim_text_sha256": "673a02b1bfa2bc17d60703a0d63894a523503de3def7822739ae645a0646fe29"}, "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "origin_evidence_ids": ["ev:83fb38120509a9368cd0d43634a3b584c7da87f0a601d37b2ba295960d6ef405"]}
{"id": "clm:8764a99fe9874a80102b7474ec1e8ff14cf437ea8ba08fe40fe1ce64b8426463", "type": "statement", "text": "Profiler delivery is best effort, and sampling can omit eligible slow operations. Absence from CloudWatch Logs therefore cannot establish that an operation was fast. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7324762659b1b2cb07b7a30597aa27e5e46112be07bb0d313eb702f6777037fc", "ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:8d83ec07f01dbba699dba48e740c89578f67795f6967af4338aadfa41eff9b84", "type": "statement", "text": "A user report (posted on AWS re:Post, and cited as a Stack Overflow question) described slow aggregate pipelines containing $lookup never appearing in DocumentDB slow query logs while other slow queries and aggregates were logged. The re:Post thread has no answers, so it gives no confirmed cause and no proof that $lookup is unsupported. (low confidence) Sources: https://repost.aws/questions/QUQEBBqG7dTPGP-t1l84EhFg/can-aws-documentdb-log-slow-aggregate-queries-containing-a-lookup-stage", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/74205235/can-aws-documentdb-log-slow-aggregate-queries-containing-a-lookup-stage", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION", "evidence_ids": [], "remediation": {"schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1", "record": "remediation.json", "requires_revalidation": true, "claim_text_sha256": "f46e0ac1af8977ffea9335160620bfa98d189ef361ff825c7cb0fa717eeb17fc"}, "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "origin_evidence_ids": ["ev:e376cad04465682ffc461ffa71e5889ac72fb17def1e840d857d5d5b5ccba241"]}
{"id": "clm:74e233865350b6dd11aa52b39e6d12fb729268b7525afe0f485814ab91cf3bda", "type": "statement", "text": "The profiler records slow-operation duration and command details in CloudWatch Logs; logged evidence can include planSummary and client metadata. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:64a54b8ff48aa011d441237f2344e679f75f6c984410809f8b4660e413514081", "type": "statement", "text": "AWS documents a default 100 ms threshold, a 50 ms minimum, and a default sampling fraction of 1.0; sampling applies to slow operations. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7324762659b1b2cb07b7a30597aa27e5e46112be07bb0d313eb702f6777037fc"]}
{"id": "clm:63e1343ea8c3b3f66fbfc92b0a8630d46b4176cfcf8c2f516f4c25b54df02eb0", "type": "statement", "text": "AWS documents best-effort delivery and requires the complete query result to fit one batch and remain under 16 MB for slow-query logging. Missing entries therefore do not prove fast execution. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0fc3aac0fa1393a8e789f707c9d1fe9d122397f8bf193bf988e8da3ba4630d31", "ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:033aee2e44736183395d1b9ebb5c42d3bc11cad08392de1d8c3473ebab6d2a99", "type": "statement", "text": "In an August 2026 production account, Castañeda used slow upsert COLLSCAN records to select indexes, then reported that those slow entries stopped appearing. This is a single incident, not a general performance guarantee. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:83fb38120509a9368cd0d43634a3b584c7da87f0a601d37b2ba295960d6ef405"]}
{"id": "clm:260abe82c9b05d65f81028136d95f4345d4482e7b2ec01c4612580b35d4faa11", "type": "statement", "text": "The profiler applies across all databases and instances in a cluster. Its records include command, duration, plan summary and client metadata. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:ab77dbfe35430ff6a8b8f7910f068389054e2ebae2e7983bb9f29e750a94bdf9", "type": "statement", "text": "CloudWatch stores profiler output under /aws/docdb/<cluster-name>/profiler, with instance-specific streams; Logs Insights can filter and rank the resulting operations. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pabis.eu/blog/2023-10-31-AWS-DocumentDB-Profiling.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a8f1b58696c91c870ed9a3e9fa81fe2fcdbee8267ff36d6250bd806c1083a7a5"]}
{"id": "clm:1eaf512dd05c207286e9caf79cbf36f4d3094559020389433b6fdac7aafc27a2", "type": "statement", "text": "Profiling uses additional cluster resources. Start with a high threshold value (for example, 500 ms) and gradually lower it; a 50 ms threshold can cause performance issues on high-throughput applications. Sources: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION", "evidence_ids": [], "remediation": {"schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1", "record": "remediation.json", "requires_revalidation": true, "claim_text_sha256": "a222ead14f701db1b380b873c2870ac70c5a49d6a40fe3170c60c8dee59b84d7"}, "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "origin_evidence_ids": ["ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b", "ev:ee2e88a97afd928715dc3a2c1fb7df00914167628ac688958d1ddec6a240c808"]}
{"id": "clm:b59e0bbc59e7b7293bce3f3b80cc994571e68e63ddc766337b1be76d0e56c11c", "type": "statement", "text": "A November 2021 Terraform AWS provider 3.61.0 issue reported recurring profiler_sampling_rate plan differences between values '1' and '1.0'. This is historical provider behavior, not evidence of a current DocumentDB profiling defect. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/issues/21679", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5c495c1be7b24d1b692b4c81c9a9e1c07a8cc4e5f792c62fbcbd6f0a4d110da5"]}
{"id": "clm:202dea2530cdff78c746d00a96f75e0e17ff3daa40ef544dea2bac8ab0b0f751", "type": "statement", "text": "Profiling applies across all databases and instances in the cluster. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8fc0912655d5ec527af9eb96c6b2ed144be0371571c8461bcc45c8e282d15c2b"]}
{"id": "clm:d7b447e29309bc28441d808121ee85db40cfb3a3916508ab630d99779d029662", "type": "statement", "text": "COLLSCAN profiler entries (planSummary \"COLLSCAN\") can point to missing indexes. The DocumentDB profiler covers update and findAndModify as well as read operations, so update operations can be inspected the same way. Sources: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/performance-slow-queries.md ; https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/profiling-slow-running-queries-in-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility ; https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/performance-slow-queries.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/", "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/profiling-slow-running-queries-in-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/developerguide/profiling.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION", "evidence_ids": [], "remediation": {"schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1", "record": "remediation.json", "requires_revalidation": true, "claim_text_sha256": "351b09063f26b8c7f7d8e60aa9c59eee4be1ecb272b2157aa55a66e338af5de2"}, "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "origin_evidence_ids": ["ev:83fb38120509a9368cd0d43634a3b584c7da87f0a601d37b2ba295960d6ef405"]}
{"id": "clm:fef8fda39ca8585cc8dbeb61dddc0e08c06a88964959aec27ad778b98ac2b64b", "type": "statement", "text": "Castañeda reports that attaching a new parameter group required instance restarts in his environment; parameter-group attachment should be evaluated separately from changing an already-active profiler parameter. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://leocasta.com/posts/when-every-write-reads-the-whole-collection/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Amazon DocumentDB profiler (CloudWatch Logs)"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:547aa140a9160eb15aa884a8f1011da788d3cd2c14fc75e93fadecf872a6268e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f6fe4837dcd2fce2676e58d4522aed97c096cba1dc35ee15b6ebe8c223da2aa4"]}
